.TH ORENDER\-WIRE 1 "2026-05-21" "openRender" "openRender User Commands"
.SH NAME
orender\-wire \- interactive RIB wireframe scene previewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B orender\-wire
.I scene.rib
.br
.B orender\-wire
.B \-\-help
.br
.B orender\-wire
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B orender\-wire
opens a RenderMan Interface Bytestream (RIB) scene file and displays all
geometry as an interactive 3-D wireframe in a GPU-accelerated native window.
.PP
On macOS the viewer is a Metal/AppKit application bundle. On Linux it uses
OpenGL 3.3 Core via GTK\~4. Both platforms share the same scene-processing
layer (\fBlibribpreview\fR) for RIB parsing and tessellation.
.PP
The initial viewpoint is taken from the camera defined in the RIB file. If no
camera is present a default perspective view framing the full scene bounding
box is synthesized.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I scene.rib
Path to the RIB file to load (required).
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary to stdout and exit 0.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version string to stdout and exit 0.
.SH CONTROLS
.SS Keyboard
.TP
.BR R ", " Home
Reset the view to the original RIB-defined camera.
.TP
.B S
Open a native save dialog to export the current camera viewpoint to a RIB file.
.TP
.B \[u2318]Q " (macOS)"
Quit.
.TP
.BR Q ", " Escape " (Linux)"
Quit.
.SS Mouse
.TP
Left button drag
Orbit — rotate around the scene center (arcball).
.TP
Scroll wheel
Zoom in / out.
.TP
Middle button drag
Pan — translate the look-at point.
.SS macOS Trackpad
.TP
Two-finger scroll
Zoom in / out.
.TP
Two-finger pan
Pan the camera.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GEOMETRIES
Optional colon-separated search path for named geometry RIB files used by the
.B Geometry
RIB statement (e.g.
.IR Geometry\ \(dqteapot\(dq ).
When unset,
.B Geometry
primitives are silently skipped and a notice is written to stderr.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
(Linux) Wayland compositor socket. Consulted by GTK\~4 when selecting the
display backend. Not read directly by
.BR orender\-wire .
.TP
.B DISPLAY
(Linux) X11 display server. Consulted by GTK\~4 when
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
is unset.
.PP
.B orender\-wire
does \fBnot\fR use
.BR ORENDERHOME ,
.BR SHADERS ,
or
.BR DISPLAYS .
Those variables are consumed by the full renderer
.RB ( orender )
and are not needed for wireframe preview.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — window opened and the user closed it normally.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error — missing or unrecognised argument.
.TP
.B 2
File not found or unreadable.
.TP
.B 3
RIB parse failed — fatal error written to stderr.
.TP
.B 4
No display available — Linux only, no X11 or Wayland server found.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
All warnings and notices are written to stderr. Stdout is silent during normal
operation.
.PP
Notable messages:
.IP \(bu 4
.BI "orender\-wire: GEOMETRIES not set, geometry '" name "' skipped"
\(em a
.B Geometry
statement was encountered but
.B GEOMETRIES
is not set.
.IP \(bu 4
.BI "orender\-wire: warning: point cloud at " id " has " N " points; displaying 100000 (subsampled)"
\(em a point cloud exceeding 100,000 points was uniformly subsampled.
.IP \(bu 4
.B "orender\-wire: warning: procedural primitive represented as bounding box"
\(em a
.B Procedural
or DSO-backed primitive is displayed as an axis-aligned bounding box.
.SH NOTES
Motion blur and deformation data are ignored; only the first time sample (t=0)
of any motion block is displayed.
.PP
Subdivision surfaces, including hierarchical subdivision meshes
.RB ( RiHierarchicalSubdivisionMesh ),
are shown as their control cage without any refinement; per-face/per-level
tag overrides on a hierarchical mesh are not resolved by the previewer and
do not affect the displayed cage.
.PP
The reference grid is drawn on the Y=0 plane of the viewer coordinate system.
RIB files authored in Z-up DCCs typically include a Y\(haZ axis-swap
.B Transform
before
.BR WorldBegin ;
this is handled transparently.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR orender (1),
.BR oshader (1),
.BR otexmake (1),
.BR rsloinfo (1)
